bader ginsburg's legacy also left a mark  here locally  so many across our community are  grieving and remembering the personal  impact she had on their lives  sasha loftis spoke with some who say her  influence was especially prominent  she joins us live near the federal  courthouse near las vegas boulevard and  bonneville with more  brian we are all feeling this loss  tonight but it was especially big for  those in the legal community  i spoke with three women of color  tonight they're all  prominent attorneys here in las vegas  and they say they wouldn't be where they  are today  if it weren't for trailblazers like rbg  and as soon as i heard i just started  screaming no no no  it was really hard it was a monumental  moment  felt around the world it was universal  everyone was looking down at their  phones everyone  had tears in their eyes after 87 years  of moving some of society's sharpest  mountains  ruth bader ginsburg lost her life on  friday  she was a champion defender for women's  rights  shaping the world as an attorney  professor and most notably  her impassioned position as a u.s  supreme court justice  she's paved the way for really all women  especially in the legal community  and so to lose her and to know that so  many of us looked up to her just felt  really personal  her influence also embodied the  landscape of las vegas  unlocking countless doors and  manifesting dreams  across our legal community she has been  a role model  i think for many women  who are lawyers and who aspire to be  just as great as she's been now as we  all commemorate the tireless steps she  took  to revolutionize our reality we're  seeing the changes that she started a  long time ago  those who loved her here at home vow to  carry  rbg's legacy close to their hearts  just give thanks to her and to people  like her  now the president of the latino bar  association here in las vegas told me  that the majority of their board right  now  is women she believes that wouldn't be  possible if it wasn't for the work  of ruth bader ginsburg reporting live  sasha loftis  8 news now
 

